With that in mind we want to develop the next phase of the work on MeTTaIL. The first step is to be able to augment rewrite rules so that their left hand side contains not only a term, but a map and the right hand side produces not only a term, but a term and a map. In this setting the maps have the following structure. The keys in the maps are spatial behavior terms refining the type of the left hand side of a rule. The values are either real numbers between 0 and 1 or complex numbers such that the absolute value of the square is between 0 and 1. These maps are used to produce Gillespie style simulators for a given program in the language defined. When the numbers are real, the Gillespie simulator is in the style of the stochastic pi-machine. When the numbers are complex the Gillespie simulator is constructed from the continuous time Markov chains for quantum model checking. Can you write these extensions for the prototype?

