Add fuzzer module to lib.rs
Now create an example that demonstrates the fuzzer with the rho-calculus:


Created a file, read a file
Created a file, read a file
Three new/updated files to add:

src/fuzzer.rs — the new module (drop into src/)
src/lib.rs — updated with pub mod fuzzer;
examples/rhocalc_fuzzer.rs — demo you can run with cargo run --example rhocalc_fuzzer
Here's how the fuzzer works:

LanguageSpec mirrors the language! macro's types and terms blocks. Each Production has a weight (default 1.0) and knows its children — simple recursive slots, binder slots (higher-order, with fresh variable generation), and variadic/bag slots.

Fuzzer::generate(sort, n, k) produces k terms of the target sort, each at most n production steps from the empty program. At each step it picks a production weighted by annotation, with a depth decay factor that progressively favors nullary productions as depth increases (ensuring termination). Inside binders, there's a configurable probability of generating a variable reference instead of a fresh sub-term.

FuzzerConfig lets you tune: depth_decay (how fast to bias toward base cases), var_ref_probability (how often to use bound variables), and variadic bounds.

The fuzz_term_to_term_ref bridge function converts fuzzed terms directly into TermRef values for the Gillespie simulator, so you get a full fuzz → simulate pipeline.

